ProsperoSunshine: the keyboard pad's profile picked by the game in front

The keyboard and mouse of a client without a controller map with the profile of the game in front: from the player's
own list, keyboard_profiles.txt next to sunshine.conf ("PPSA01234 = driving" per line, any title ID including homebrew
and forwarders, and profiles of their own in [name] sections), and with keyboard_mouse_profile_by_game = 1 (off by
default) from the title map tools/title_profiles.py makes from Wikidata, by title ID, the Store concept in param.json,
or the English name. Anything else keeps keyboard_mouse_profile, and with no game running (none open, not even
suspended behind the home screen) it is the menu keys, standard's with W A S D on the D-pad, whatever the profile. The
running title (sceLncUtilGetAppIdOfRunningBigApp, through ps_title_running) is looked up at most every two seconds
while the keys and mouse are in use, the list read anew when it changes; a new profile lets go of what the old one
held.

